# Graphify is for SOURCE CODE only (deterministic AST, refreshed for free by the
# git hooks). Markdown -- CLAUDE.md, PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md, docs/ -- is read
# directly as plain text and NEVER indexed: indexing it cost an LLM pass on every
# edit and let the graph contradict the docs (ADR-13 in the backend memory repo,
# memory-bank/lessonsLearned.md). This replaces the old !CLAUDE.md and !docs/
# negations, which existed only to index those files.
*.md
docs/
memory-bank/

# Angular templates too: graphify has no AST extractor for them and treats them
# as documents (an LLM pass that goes stale on every UI change). The template <->
# component bindings they described are checked exactly by the Angular compiler
# (`ng build` fails on a broken binding), so the graph keeps only the deterministic
# TypeScript side. With this, nothing in this repo reaches graphify's LLM path.
*.html
